<h2 id="learnuitbl-ui" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. UI conventions</h2>

- **Chips:** `GenderChipBar` — one active chip; default to the learner’s first skill (e.g. suffix patterns).
- **Tables:** `LearnGroupedTable` chrome — blue `.learn-table-head-cell` header; `.learn-table-row--g0…g7` bands from **Grouping Note** / `groupOrder` (`% 8`, first-seen order if omitted); title column `.learn-table-cell--accent` (auto-first column if none marked); trailing **Grouping Note** column (≤4 words per group). Prefer group palette over gender-only row tints. **MUI:** tint **cells** (`.learn-table-row--gN > .MuiTableCell-root`), not only `<tr>` — otherwise accent text rotates while row fills look identical.
- **Determiners:** all four tabs (`demonstratives`, `contractions`, `crase`, `register`) — `determinersTableBuild.ts` for group order/labels.
- **Queued areas (same pattern):** Verb patterns · Comparatives · Numbers · Clitics.
- **Places atlas:** Article · Name · Learn as · Example · Note.
- **Locative tab:** ≤5 chips (Countries · States & cities · Home & shops · Stacked places · From & to); one `LearnGroupedTable` per chip; `placeUsageLocativeConfig.ts` maps API categories; persist `locative` chip in filter hook. **Data:** curated `place_usage_rule_seeds.py` only (guide §5) — do not blind-import `Article+Places` workbook rows.
- **Animated Same form:** pattern table **or** vocab list — never both showing the same suffix block.

